        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.087,
            0.881,
            0.129
          ],
          "content": "？ **Like the triangle inequality, can you form a rule that describes the two angles for which a triangle is possible?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.139,
            0.831,
            0.157
          ],
          "content": "**Ans**: Rules for two angles A and B to form a triangle is $0^{\\circ} <  A  +  B  < 180^{\\circ}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.192,
            0.252,
            0.209
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 165**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.221,
            0.299,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": "？ **Figure it out**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.133,
            0.251,
            0.882,
            0.293
          ],
          "content": "**1. Find the third angle of a triangle (using a parallel line) when two of the angles are:**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.163,
            0.304,
            0.541,
            0.322
          ],
          "content": "**Process for (a) is given. Try for rest.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.332,
            0.288,
            0.35
          ],
          "content": "(a) $\\mathbf { 3 6 ^ { \\circ } } , 7 2 ^ { \\circ }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.332,
            0.357,
            0.673,
            0.515
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_32_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.525,
            0.881,
            0.565
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:**Consider $\\Delta \\mathrm { A B C } ,$ , Draw line XY parallel to line BC so AB and AC become transversals."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.2,
            0.576,
            0.86,
            0.594
          ],
          "content": "Therefore $\\angle XAB = \\angle B = 36^{\\circ}$ and $\\angle YAC = \\angle C = 72^{\\circ}$ (Alternate Angles)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.2,
            0.605,
            0.336,
            0.622
          ],
          "content": "On line XY —"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.2,
            0.634,
            0.489,
            0.65
          ],
          "content": "\\angle XAB + \\angle BAC + \\angle YAC = 180^{\\circ}",
          "image_source": "images/page_32_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.2,
            0.663,
            0.349,
            0.679
          ],
          "content": "So,  BAC = 72°"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.697,
            0.301,
            0.714
          ],
          "content": "(b) $\\mathbf { 1 5 0 ^ { \\circ } } , \\mathbf { 1 5 ^ { \\circ } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.72,
            0.263,
            0.737
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** $1 5 ^ { \\circ }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.758,
            0.287,
            0.775
          ],
          "content": "(c) $\\mathbf { 9 0 ^ { \\circ } , 3 0 ^ { \\circ } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.782,
            0.262,
            0.798
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** $6 0 ^ { \\circ }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.819,
            0.289,
            0.836
          ],
          "content": "(d) $7 5 ^ { \\circ } , 4 5 ^ { \\circ }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.843,
            0.262,
            0.859
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** 60°"
        },
